# shir_nodes/case_transform.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# Lowercase/uppercase transform (lowered from `tr`, `${var,,}`, `${var^^}`).
#
# Backends: Perl lc/uc, JS toLowerCase/toUpperCase, C tolower/toupper, Rust to_lowercase
# Fallback: sh2.caseTransform(text, upper)
#
# ShIR_TextOps_Strings proves `case_transform_sound` over the BYTE table: length is
# preserved, casing is idempotent, `uc` after `lc` is `uc` and vice versa, and every
# byte above 127 is a fixed point. OUT OF MODEL: non-ASCII casing. The model cases
# ASCII letters only, so `[0xC3, 0xA9]` (U+00E9) is left alone; Rust `to_uppercase`,
# JS `toUpperCase` and Perl `uc` under `use utf8` case-map the CODE POINT and return
# U+00C9. A renderer is faithful only with an ASCII guard, which is why the node does
# not promise a language's full casing table (see the theory section's closing text).

node CaseTransform
tag "CaseTransform"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field text: expr
field upper: bool
spec: TextOps#case_transform_sound
